Container narrow detail columns (2026-10-24)
============================================

- Preserve dynamic detail tab lists when a valid narrow column is 30 pixels or
  less; retain the zero-width guard and add a narrow-layout regression.
- Keep the existing per-call tab ownership and public Container behavior; see
  docs/container-tabs.md.

Non-text Unicode widget qualification (2026-10-24)
===================================================

- Add an installed-prefix Xvfb matrix for Label, List and ComboBox values,
  covering combining marks, a non-BMP character and Han text through their
  public XmString and selection APIs.
- Record the round-trip and selection contract in docs/nontext-unicode.md.

Container dynamic tab-list ownership (2026-10-24)
==================================================

- Replace the static process-global detail-tab pool with checked per-call
  storage, releasing temporary tabs after tab-list insertion while preserving
  the public Container and XmTabList contracts.
- Add an Xvfb regression covering two independent detail Containers; see
  docs/container-tabs.md.

Reject unrepresentable text-source ranges (2026-10-24)
=======================================================

- Validate XmTextPosition ranges and allocation sizes before conversion;
  reject positions that cannot cross the legacy int-indexed source reader,
  and cap internal blocks without truncating arithmetic.
- Add installed-prefix boundary coverage for valid extraction and oversized
  ranges; preserve existing byte/wide-character results for representable
  requests. See docs/text-source-bounds.md.
Checked image scaling dimensions and strides (2026-10-24)
===========================================================

- Reject invalid image rectangles, non-finite or unrepresentable scaling
  ratios, overflowing destination dimensions, row strides and coordinate-table
  sizes before rendering. Use unsigned intermediate coordinates so legacy
  Position and Dimension narrowing cannot corrupt scaled output.
- Add native overflow and malformed-image regression coverage and document the
  installed-prefix runner; ordinary pixmap cache and rendering APIs remain
  compatible.
UIL debug listing formatter bounds (2026-10-24)
===============================================

- Replace the fixed-buffer vsprintf path in debug UIL listings with measured,
  owned formatting and bounded line emission. Long generated text no longer
  overwrites listing state or trips the debug assertion.
- Add a long-output regression and document the debug validation command; the
  public UIL command-line and release listing behavior remain compatible.
DataField invalid wide-text conversion (2026-10-24)
===================================================

- Keep the owned conversion buffer when DataField access-text handling receives
  an unrepresentable wide character. The existing empty-value fallback now
  completes without freeing static storage or terminating the client.
- Preserve valid locale conversion, trait and resource contracts, callbacks,
  widget layouts and native ABI. Add a native access-text trait regression for
  valid and invalid wide values; see docs/datafield-wide-text.md.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the DataField regression and installed ABI,
  SpinBox, List Unicode and DPI widget regressions. The unchanged prior library
  aborts on the invalid-wide-character case.

ComboBox selection after final-item deletion (2026-10-24)
========================================================

- Select the surviving final item when XmComboBoxDeletePos removes the selected
  last item from a nonempty list, instead of passing its now-invalid old index
  to the List. Synchronize displayed text, selected resources and the existing
  replacement-selection callback, as with first/middle-item deletion.
- Preserve one-based deletion positions and the zero-as-last alias, configured
  zero/one-based resource and callback positions, unselected-item behavior,
  public interfaces, widget layouts and native ABI. Add a native 408-case matrix
  across all three ComboBox types and both position modes; see
  docs/combo-deletion.md.
- Native AArch64 validation passes all 408 cases and 5,880 checks; the unchanged
  prior library fails the selected-last deletion case. Installed ABI, SpinBox,
  List Unicode, DPI, PanedWindow and button-timer regressions also pass.

PanedWindow keyboard movement cancellation (2026-10-24)
======================================================

- Keep one pending keyboard sash timeout when opposite directions cancel the
  movement total to zero. Use the existing timeout ID to identify pending work,
  so further keys do not overwrite it with an additional timeout.
- Preserve batching timing, default/large increments, resources, action
  parameters, widget layouts and native ABI. Add native horizontal/vertical
  regressions for cancellation, movement, fresh batches and pending destruction;
  see docs/paned-keyboard.md.
- Native AArch64 validation passes 1,072 checks; the unchanged prior library
  fails the same fixture on duplicate scheduling. Installed ABI, SpinBox, List
  Unicode, DPI and button-timer regressions also pass.

Keyboard button release-animation lifetime (2026-10-24)
======================================================

- Keep one pending release-animation timeout in ArrowButton, ArrowButtonGadget
  and push-enabled DrawnButton during repeated keyboard activation, matching
  PushButton and PushButtonGadget. Destruction can then cancel the owned timeout
  instead of leaving earlier callbacks scheduled against a retired widget.
- Preserve every activation callback, public resources, callback data, instance
  layouts and native ABI. Add a native regression covering repeated activation
  and destruction in all five button classes; see docs/button-timers.md.
- Native AArch64 validation passes 630 checks. The unchanged prior library fails
  the same fixture on its duplicate-timer assertion. Installed ABI, SpinBox,
  List Unicode and DPI regressions pass against the independent fixed build.

Native composition state query (2026-10-24)
==========================================

- Add XmTextHasPreedit for Text and TextField. This nonmutating public query
  reports active native preedit, including empty composition and verification,
  without resetting XIM or exposing temporary composition bytes as committed
  application input. NULL and other widget classes return False.
- Add a focused native state-query regression covering independent controls,
  repeated queries, verification and unchanged source bytes. This controls
  native state records and does not claim live input-method acceptance.
- Native ARM64 installed qualification passes the 63-assertion getter fixture,
  ABI, existing preedit/local-compose fixtures and 79-assertion font lifetime.

Native Unicode hard lines, geometry and retained output (2026-10-24)
====================================================================

- Recognize complete CRLF and mandatory Unicode hard-line separators in native
  UTF-8 source scans/counts without modifying stored bytes or scalar positions.
  Cross whole terminators during visual motion and restart wrapped line-table
  reflow at the current hard paragraph after accepted edits. This prevents an
  old line start inside a newly formed CRLF from being shaped across paragraphs.
  Custom scanners and non-UTF-8 native source policies remain distinct.
- Treat NODELTA as geometry invalidation, retiring cached captures instead of
  adding LONG_MAX to source positions during source replacement or resize.
- Honor explicitly supplied width/height during font changes even when equal to
  current dimensions; derive omitted dimensions from rows/columns independently.
  Refresh global and visible line geometry before cursor/IM queries and native
  navigator notifications, using current font state after callbacks.
- Add independently retained immutable output captures and saturating counters
  of actual paragraph analysis, HarfBuzz shaping and line capture work. Internal
  opaque objects change; existing widget records and ABI epoch 8 stay unchanged.
- Add the incremental-layout native regression: shared sources, retained/rebased
  unaffected captures, mandatory separators, CRLF joins/splits, distant bidi
  context, wrap/font/configuration changes, dimension authority and auto sizing.
  Compare real native output against fresh widgets for source ranges, glyphs,
  wrapping, carets, hits, selections and actual glyph pixels. Include incremental
  source-map/widget/layout fixtures in source distribution metadata.
- Normal AArch64 qualification passes all 33 selected native fixtures. The new
  regression passes 12,890,100 assertions/417 native-fresh line comparisons with
  zero layout warnings; negative controls expose the prior faults. It measures
  reuse of unaffected hard paragraphs, not incremental shaping within an edited
  paragraph or complete interactive editor/input acceptance.
- Strict ASan/UBSan completes that regression body but its exit leak gate still
  reports 208 bytes in two Xt selection-context allocations. A separate strict
  font-lifetime fixture passes 79 assertions across two displays, zero X errors.
  An additional strict legacy layout probe reports Fontconfig allocations, so
  broad sanitizer acceptance is not claimed. No suppression or disabled leak
  detection is used. See docs/status.md and docs/unicode.md for qualification.

