Publication and acceptance policy (2026-10-24)
====================================================================

Bug fixes require relevant passing automated regression tests before publication.
Record accepted fixes here and update relevant docs/ pages. Commit and push
accepted fixes to both rpi4 and GitHub independently of consuming applications'
gates, development phases or dependency pins. See AGENTS.md for the full policy.
This policy entry does not assert acceptance of unfinished source changes.

Committed native correctness updates through 7376266 (2026-10-24)
====================================================================

- 7376266: Retain immutable incremental Unicode source indexes, sharing
  unaffected paragraphs and publishing accepted edits atomically. Correct
  TextField callback scratch ownership, wide-character whole-value verification,
  approved replacement/deletion and rejected/reentrant proposal handling.
  Native widget regressions and allocation-failure tests cover these paths.
  Native record changes require a coordinated rebuild for ABI epoch 8.
- c9f2678: Resolve semantic WINDOW coordinates through the native shell while
  retaining immediate-parent PARENT coordinates; reject invalid bounds and
  targets retired during origin queries. Native regressions cover independent
  shells and reentrant removal. Separately qualify existing local Compose input.
- 8d4ea25, 225139a: Correct render-table ownership and resources belonging to
  independent displays; release label shadow GCs during appearance replacement.
- 250a30d, d382adb, dbca66e: Respect ancestor clipping and label ownership in
  accessibility; preserve empty compound strings without invalid byte operations;
  supply complete native callback data for semantic button activation.
- b364c0e, 6804e18: Apply native modal input scope to accessibility mutations and
  correct primary-window modality while preserving nested grab scopes.
- 9a3b1da, 5a0ab20: Bound explicit private IBus engine admission and repair XIM
  transport lifetime and composition ordering. Native service/input fixtures
  document their exact accepted scenarios and remaining coverage limits.
- 20955b2, 5f18b5b: Expose stable native List selection with reentrant lifetime
  guards; qualify allocation-failure behavior separately from instrumentation.
- c1f5c4b, 278ee12, 6be3d36, 8f58bad: Forward native keyboard events to
  synchronous accessibility listeners; report exact text edits, menu semantics,
  initial state and selections; index live trees and implement AT-SPI cache and
  text boundaries with native regression coverage.
- b726c1d, a5130d9: Correct the Xt INCR lifetime dependency and exercise native
  Unicode clipboard and interrupted incremental transfers. These corrections
  do not assert acceptance of every outstanding Xt selection/lifetime issue.
- aa00878, 6b0a873: Release replaced WML literals, bound string-generator comment
  parsing and release generator metadata.
- 2bdd848, 74cf650, 46c7957, 1c1638e: Advance the native epoch for font contexts
  and numeric providers, use documented Xft column metrics, bound per-widget
  font/shaping caches and expose native scrollbar values to accessibility.
- 96485e8, b4c2a27, 35d0829, b9cd24a: Correct fixture counts and document runtime,
  sanitizer, installed-ABI and native validation prerequisites and limits.

See docs/history.md, docs/unicode.md and docs/status.md for contracts and detailed
qualification boundaries. Passing focused regressions is not a claim that all
native input, editor or sanitizer scenarios are accepted; inherited Xt context
leaks remain explicitly unaccepted. Uncommitted hard-line/reflow work is excluded
from this entry.

